WEBVTT

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.740
So hot...

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.170
Not even 8:00 and it feels 
like my body's gonna melt!

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.840
BM!

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.980
Would you stop with those 
stifling capital letters!

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.720
You're just making it hotter!

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.530
EM, <i>excuse me</i>?!

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.400
I'm telling you to cut that out!

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.930
Forget it! This is my policy. MP, yo!

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.170
It's annoying!

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.170
<i>What?!</i>

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:39.910
Hey! Quit hogging the way!

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.060
Shut up!

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.910
What was that?!

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.220
K-Kamui the Great!

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.250
What are <i>you</i> doing here?!

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.570
You guys are taking the train, 
right? I thought I'd see you off.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:54.890
More importantly, don't fight over 
trivial stuff first thing in the morning!

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.490
You're spoiling the beautiful weather!

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.270
BW, you say?!

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.790
Aren't you hot, Kamui the Great?

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.300
Of <i>course</i> I'm hot!

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.970
But there's nothin' wrong with being hot!

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:08.430
Baloney!

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.270
This is what they call the Summer Battle!

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:13.910
That's right...

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:15.470
SB, yo...

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:19.460
Yeah! It's the start of the 
long-awaited national championship!

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:55.190
The train, huh? I feel sluggish...

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:59.510
You're lucky, Kamui the Great, gettin' 
a ride to the tournament hall...

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:03.120
I wouldn't mind givin' you a 
lift, but in that rattletrap...

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:13.520
Certainly, in the van, it'll be you, Aichi, 
the girl who works in the store, and...

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.740
...that jerk, Kai, so between 
all of you and your bags,

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.450
there probably wouldn't 
be any spare room, right?

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:21.090
Don't even mention that creep's name!

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.270
You mean Kai?

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:30.030
Yeah! Here I've got into nationals, but when I 
think that I'm goin' with him, my joy is half gone!

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.490
A Stormy Beginning! The National Championship!

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.700
Good morning, Brother!

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.740
'Morning, Kamui!

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.830
It looks like we're all here.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.350
Then shall we go?

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:55.890
I call shotgun!

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.960
No, no, you can't have the passenger seat.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.420
Misaki sits there.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.590
He says he needs me there to navigate.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:07.200
If you don't know the roads, buy 
a GPS, you bad-at-everything!

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:08.120
Is that right?

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.320
Do you want to say "good-for-nothing"?

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.710
Yeah, that's it!

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:15.100
Do you think a GPS is 
necessary with Misaki here?

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.040
W-Well, no...

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:18.570
Yeesh...

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:23.060
Tch! Whatever! Then I get 
the back window seat!

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.790
W-Why, <i>you</i>...!

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:28.490
What?

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.220
That's <i>my</i> seat!

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.030
Why?

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:37.510
I-I've always gotten the window 
seat, ever since I was born!

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.460
Like I care.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:46.050
Kamui, look, there's another window 
seat here. This is fine, right?

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.190
Let's roll!

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:04.330
Turn right there.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.310
Sure!

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.140
I said <i>right</i>!

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:17.460
You're a lousy driver!

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.310
I'm alive again!

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:39.950
Wow!

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:41.160
Awesome!

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.110
Shin, this is the back entrance.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:49.690
The regional tournament was impressive, 
but this tournament hall is even bigger!

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:52.290
Well, sure, it's the <i>national</i> championship.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:55.800
Because of that, the parking 
lot is already full...

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:02.240
I'll park the car somewhere, so please 
wait around here a bit, you guys.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:03.000
Okay!

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:08.210
Seems like it'll be a while 
before he gets back...

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:10.010
Guess all we can do is 
kick back and wait, huh?

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.390
Yep.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:13.560
Okay!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.400
What's going on over there?

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.780
TV cameras!

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:21.970
Today's tournament will be 
broadcast live all over the country!

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:23.490
Really?

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.530
They always broadcast 
the national tournament live.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.110
Haven't you ever seen it?

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.220
N-No...

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:32.930
Now that I look closely, isn't that Dr. O?!

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:38.360
Maybe this is Vanguard TV on location!

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:41.350
Brother, let's go check it out!

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:45.250
That's not something you 
get to see every day!

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.270
Come on, hurry up!

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.220
Kamui!

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:50.540
Oww...

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.170
Sorry! Are you okay?!

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:52.930
Kamui!

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.390
<i>The History of Rome</i>?

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:01.000
Kamui, are you all right?

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.130
I'm fine, Brother!

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:04.200
Thank goodness!

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:08.430
You don't say "thank goodness" 
after you slam into someone!

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.110
I thought I was hit by a Mack truck!

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.780
Sorry, sorry!

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.380
But you ran into me...

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:17.580
Anyway, I'm just happy you're not hurt.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:18.830
Sorry.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.460
M-Me too...

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.690
I'm sorry, I was looking the other way!

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:24.880
Please pardon us!

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.880
What are you doing, Koutei?

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.430
Did something happen?

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:30.510
I had a little collision...

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:34.090
Sorry, kid. Are you okay?

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.520
K-Kid?!

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.490
Don't treat me like a child!

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:40.690
You're bleeding. You must've 
scraped your elbow.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:43.150
Hold on a second. I should have a band-aid.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.220
I-It's no big deal!

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:48.160
Then he <i>was</i> injured?

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.090
I really am sorry.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.430
Never mind!

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:51.120
Here.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.360
Thank you!

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:57.600
There you are!

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:59.870
Don't expect any thanks...

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.510
Oh, I don't care about <i>that</i>!

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:03.920
Child...

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:11.930
Because of <i>you</i>, we missed the location shoot!

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:14.460
Sorry, sorry!

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.310
I'm so sorry...

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:18.140
He's nice to a fault...

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.450
Those kids...

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:23.940
I wonder what they're doing.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.670
Looks like there's trouble...

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:28.520
Are they going to be alright 
in today's tournament like that?

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:29.490
We'll see...

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:29.940
Oh!

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:33.030
They're suddenly becoming 
acquainted with <i>that</i> team...

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.780
Team Caesar?!

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.550
Are they famous?

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.030
What are you saying?!

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:43.630
Last year, they won second place and the 
year before that, they were the champions!

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:45.380
The champions?!

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:48.150
It's Team Caesar!

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:51.030
Look! It's Kenji Mitsusada!

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.650
Next to him is Gai Usui 
and his big sister, Yuri!

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:56.480
I hear they won the regional 
tournament hands-down!

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:59.850
Sorry, but could we take this somewhere else?

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.340
I'm just not comfortable 
being the center of attention.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:09.690
They're a former champion team...

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:12.440
Our bags!

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.690
Sorry! Please wait a second!

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:18.010
Is this one of those "fateful encounters"?!

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.460
It's just a coincidence.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.570
Fate or chance?

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:25.160
We'll know the answer to that, too, 
by the time this tournament is over.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.320
Right.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:27.890
What do you mean?

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:30.340
Here's fine.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:32.850
Can't you do anything about your nature?

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:34.900
I really don't care to stand out...

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:37.970
Even though it doesn't faze you when 
you're having a Vanguard fight...

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.950
You're a wonder.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.880
Well, why don't we introduce 
ourselves properly?

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:47.880
I'm the leader of Team 
Caesar, Kenji Mitsusada.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.510
I'm Yuri Usui.

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:51.570
I'm her younger brother, Gai.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:53.970
Huh? Kenji Mitsusada?

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:56.580
Didn't they call you by 
a different name before?

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.270
Oh, right, "Koutei"!

00:09:58.270 --> 00:09:59.330
"Koutei"?

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:02.320
Uh-huh! The alternative kanji 
readings of Mitsusada, "Koutei"!

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:04.840
皇帝 = Emperor

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:04.840
Oh, the direct pronunciation of the Kanji characters!

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:07.710
I see. That's why you're 
called "Team Caesar".

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.190
What are you talking about?

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:13.460
"Caesar" was the title of 
the ancient Roman emperor.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:20.360
The origin of that name is Gaius Julius 
Caesar, who was assassinated in an untimely manner...

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:21.780
You're running at the mouth!

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:24.440
And I was just getting to 
the interesting part...

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:27.820
Nobody's asking about your 
wealth of historical knowledge.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:31.070
Then let me at least tell 
them about Octavius...

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:32.360
Sorry!

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:37.950
Anyway, we named our team Caesar 
after the Roman emperor.

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:39.390
That's the long and short of it.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:40.380
Cool!

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:44.790
Kourin!

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:46.830
Morikawa?!

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:52.960
Now my tournament hall limited edition 
goods collection is complete!

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.170
I achieved what I set out to do today!

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:56.610
Good for you...

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:58.560
<i>What</i> did you come here for?!

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:01.480
Cheering on Team Q4 takes a back seat?

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.500
It's apples and oranges.

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:07.770
This also means a huge boost to 
my Ultra-rare fan club points!

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.310
And I'm ready to cheer them on with bells on!

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.640
There's nothing wrong with my way of life!

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:15.570
Hey, Aichi! I'm here!

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.160
Are you done?

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.340
What was that?!

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:23.280
Well, in a way, you let me slacks, Lose-umi.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.400
<i>Relax</i>...

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:27.030
"Relax", that's what I said, isn't it?

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:28.190
Sure.

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:31.460
Come to think of it, Reiji 
and Eiji aren't here.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:35.580
Don't tell me they got on the wrong train...

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:40.310
Well, if Lose-umi made it, I'm 
sure they'll show up soon.

00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:41.310
Right.

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:43.740
Knock it off! I'm <i>Katsumi</i>!

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:44.990
It's about time you remembered that!

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:46.700
You think he could hear me?

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.810
No, probably just instinct...

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:50.680
Whoa...

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:52.120
I know...

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.950
Huh? Feels like we've forgotten something...

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:57.290
Hey, everyone!

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:59.290
Where'd you go?!

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:26.310
Enthusiastic curiosity

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:29.330
Be strong and decide

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:34.770
Running heart, which are you watching?

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:40.060
I want to expand my capacity for excitement

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:44.780
and be thrilled every single day!

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:48.210
Bargaining is an iffy thing

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:50.790
It's all about luck

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:56.890
That, too, is included in 
everything, and it's all me!

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:59.680
You're serious and that's why

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.310
You'll be able to smile

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:04.720
Kourin!

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.750
Come on, you guys too, let 
her hear your support!

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:08.850
Me too?!

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.340
Naturally!

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.720
That's why we're here!

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:14.020
It is <i>not</i>!

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:18.070
This year's opening ceremony 
sure has razzmatazz!

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:20.140
Was it different before?

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:25.140
Yeah. There was a lot of fanfare, 
but it wasn't as boisterous as this.

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:27.360
They didn't have anything like 
a concert from an idol group.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:31.480
I don't care for all this noise myself.

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:36.040
But it's making some people 
happy, so what's the harm?

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.350
Did I hear someone say <i>people</i>?

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:41.050
Kourin!

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:43.510
Nonsense...

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:48.480
You just said "nonsense", 
didn't you, scumbag?!

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:49.680
Morikawa!

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.140
Nobody said that!!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.000
R-Really?

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:56.690
I could've sworn I heard that... 
Maybe just my imagination...

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:02.260
Oh, he said it. We couldn't hear 
it, but I'm positive he said it!

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:04.530
This guy's a riot!

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.090
By the way...

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:10.660
There are four on your team, so have 
you decided who's going to fight?

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:15.580
Is your strategy to change the team 
order according to your opponent?

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:18.580
Or do you have other ideas?

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.760
Well...

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:25.870
That's right. Just like at 
the regional tournament,

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:28.060
today it'll be teams of three 
fighting against each other.

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:32.540
Misaki wasn't there last time, 
so I participated, but...

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:35.600
among these members, I'm not really...

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:37.280
Stop it, Gai.

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:40.470
Don't be so nosy about 
another team's strategy.

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:42.710
Nope, doesn't really matter.

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:48.320
'Cause we don't even call it a strategy.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.330
It's simple.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:53.120
The weakest player amongst 
the four of us gets left out.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:54.830
That's all.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:55.720
Kai!

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:56.340
What?

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:59.250
Moron! Ever heard of something called <i>tact</i>?!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.780
No fighting, you two!

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:04.140
Leave us alone!

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:07.050
This problem is between the members of Q4!

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.170
S-Sure...

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.300
Problem?

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.550
That's right. It is a problem.

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:12.900
Why, you!

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:14.090
Wait, Kamui!

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:15.120
Brother!

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:17.390
It's okay. I'll bow out.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.950
The weakest fighter is left out.

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:24.270
What Kai said is right.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:27.990
And the weakest fighter in Team Q4 is...

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:29.400
me.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:31.910
Brother...

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:34.240
Then it's settled.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:39.330
Kai, answer one question!

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:44.060
What is Vanguard to you?!

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:48.020
Searching for someone who's stronger 
and beating that person in battle.

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:51.630
That's my Vanguard.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.210
That's all?!

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:56.390
Yeah.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:58.850
I see...

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:09.320
Originally, I didn't go to Card 
Capital because I liked it...

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:14.010
It's just that I didn't want 
to be part of Team Handsome...

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:16.740
so I started dropping by out of necessity.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:22.250
What I'm saying is that I didn't have 
especially strong feelings for Team Q4.

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:27.870
But now I think we've got a good team!

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.750
I wanna win with this team!

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:33.590
But <i>you</i>...

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:36.090
It was the same situation previously...

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:39.060
Anybody who wants to quit should quit.

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:40.990
Kai...?

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:43.150
<i>Everyone</i> has a past.

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:47.740
Using that as a perpetual reason for your 
own weakness is childish, pure and simple.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:51.970
You don't even think twice about 
telling people to quit or drop out...!

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:58.930
Kai, what do you think 
a teammate really is?!

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.630
I have no interest in that.

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:04.490
No matter what I think, it does not affect 
the outcome, does it?

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:06.280
<i>You...!!</i>

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:07.130
Kamui!

00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:10.780
I can't take it anymore!

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:11.860
Kamui...?

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.930
Brother, I'm sorry, but I...

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:19.510
I can't fight alongside him anymore.

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:20.970
So I...

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:22.600
I'm sorry!

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:23.720
Kamui!

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:24.740
Kamui!

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:27.170
What's going on?

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:28.060
What's wrong?!

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:32.530
Oh, good. This is where you guys have been.

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.460
I've been searching high and low for you guys!

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:35.910
I'm sorry, Manager.

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:37.550
I'm kind of in a hurry!

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:39.810
Where are you going?

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:41.460
The tournament's about to start!

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:44.460
The concert is over,

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:48.610
so right after they draw for the initial 
match-ups, the first round will start.

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:50.760
It's gonna start already?!

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:54.880
Let's go, Tokura.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:58.950
Come on, Aichi.

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:01.480
Kai...

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:07.390
If you don't come, on top of Katsuragi's 
disappearance, Team Q4 forfeits.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.760
Do you want that?

00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:10.430
Kamui? Forfeit?

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:12.780
Did something happen?

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:13.480
You got me.

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:14.550
No idea.

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:15.630
I dunno.

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:18.500
Can I say something?

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:20.300
Koutei?

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:27.760
Did you know that the national tournament 
is held on two days, today and next week?

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:28.970
Y-Yes?

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:32.710
The elimination rounds take 
place today, the first day.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:38.880
So if you win today, you'll be able to 
advance to the final tournament a week from now.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:46.940
Right now, instead of chasing after him, 
maybe you should get through the preliminaries...

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:49.820
and secure a place for him to come back to.

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:51.920
Kamui...

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:56.230
How about it? I think that's 
what teams are all about.

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:57.990
Yeah.

00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:03.290
This is the rear entrance, isn't it?!

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:06.910
RE, yo! Who's the one that knew a shortcut?!

00:19:08.770 --> 00:19:11.450
It's probably already started!

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:15.880
NP, no problem! There's still time 
before the first fight starts...

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:17.390
Kamui the Great?!

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:20.690
Please wait up!

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:23.690
Where are you going, Kamui the Great?!

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:26.910
I'm beat.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:29.930
Oh, yeah? I like singing.

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:32.680
It's not like I hate it, but...

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:34.270
Oh, I see! It's age!

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:35.330
Shut up!

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:39.560
Keep mouthing off and I'll 
take <i>your</i> part, Rekka!

00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:41.410
No, don't you dare!

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:41.900
Huh?

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:42.630
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:43.780
What is it?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:47.360
Those kids...

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:49.450
Could they be...

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:50.650
...having a falling out?

00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:55.700
There's no time 'til your next 
appearance, so please get ready!

00:19:55.700 --> 00:19:56.500
Okay!

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.090
Let's hurry up!

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:06.220
And now, the master of ceremonies 
you all know and love...

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:08.780
me, MC Miya!

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:12.170
I don't know you! Get off 
the stage, you two-bit MC!

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:17.940
Square glasses, we don't need any boring MC!

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:20.540
Just bring out Ultra-rare!

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:21.980
Morikawa!

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:23.950
You hurt me...

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.770
Get Kourin out here!

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:27.980
H-Hey!

00:20:27.980 --> 00:20:29.850
Get that little finger down!

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:31.300
You too?!

00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:33.270
You little...

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:37.540
And now, let's give a warm welcome...

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.290
to my assistants for today!

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:42.290
Ultra-rare!

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:43.450
If you please!

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:53.450
I've been waiting for you, Kourin!

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:54.710
You've been <i>waiting</i>...?

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:56.750
Only for about 10 minutes, right?

00:20:56.750 --> 00:21:01.060
For me, that 10 minutes feels 
like 10 years! Understand?

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:02.110
Yeah, yeah...

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:05.620
Today is a perfect day 
for Vanguard, isn't it?

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:06.510
Uh-huh!

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:09.380
All right, everyone, let's 
give it up for Vanguard!

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:14.670
Let's stay psyched and have 
a good time with Vanguard!

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:21.730
Let's fight! Let's Vanguard!

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:29.890
For starters, it looks like you 
didn't have to forfeit, right?

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:33.420
Koutei, you really are a meddler.

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:38.900
Let's leave it at that. His meddling and his strong 
fighting ability are his only redeeming features.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:41.450
That's a little harsh.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:43.830
Even if you are right...

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:04.760
Wait for us, Kamui...

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:11.010
We'll make it through the preliminary 
rounds, then come and get you.

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:16.950
To bring you back to Team Quadrifoglio...

00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:55.400
I hope Kamui comes back...

00:23:55.400 --> 00:23:57.930
Remember what the guy from Team Caesar said?

00:23:58.460 --> 00:24:00.120
Oh, that's right.

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:03.470
I have to do my best to win so Kamui 
has a place to come back to...

00:24:03.470 --> 00:24:04.250
Yes.

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:06.320
I'll try my best, too.

00:24:06.320 --> 00:24:07.750
Thank you, Misaki!

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:10.150
Next time: Jurassic Army!

00:24:10.150 --> 00:24:14.100
I win the first match, then you 
and Kai win yours, Misaki...

00:24:14.100 --> 00:24:15.950
I can totally picture it...

00:24:15.950 --> 00:24:17.880
Aichi Sendou will do his best!
